## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to implement a cross-topic enrichment pattern with per-key state management, handle late-arriving data, and ensure at-least-once semantics with idempotent outputs.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-topic join by userId
- Windowing: 5-minute hopping window with 2-minute late-arrival tolerance
- Per-key state store with TTL-based eviction
- Idempotent outputs to prevent duplicates across restarts
- EnrichmentStore API exposure for testing and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
class CrossTopicEnrichmentSink {
  constructor(windowSize = 5 * 60 * 1000, lateTolerance = 2 * 60 * 1000) {
    this.store = new Map();
    this.emittedKeys = new Set();
    this.windowSize = windowSize;
    this.lateTolerance = lateTolerance;
  }

  onMessage(ctx, msg) {
    const { topic, userId, timestamp, data } = msg;
    const key = `${topic}:${userId}:${this.getWindowId(timestamp)}`;

    if (this.emittedKeys.has(key)) return;

    if (!this.store.has(userId)) {
      this.store.set(userId, { clicks: [], impressions: [], firstSeen: Date.now() });
    }

    const buffer = this.store.get(userId);
    buffer[topic].push({ ...data, timestamp });

    this.tryEnrich(userId, key);
  }

  tryEnrich(userId, key) {
    const buffer = this.store.get(userId);
    if (buffer.clicks.length > 0 && buffer.impressions.length > 0) {
      const enriched = {
        userId,
        clicks: buffer.clicks,
        impressions: buffer.impressions,
        enrichedAt: Date.now()
      };
      this.emittedKeys.add(key);
      buffer.clicks = [];
      buffer.impressions = [];
      return enriched;
    }
  }

  getWindowId(timestamp) {
    return Math.floor(timestamp / this.windowSize);
  }

  commitOffsets() {
    this.emittedKeys.clear();
  }

  enrichmentStore() {
    return this.store;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assess the candidate's ability to design per-tenant fairness in a high-throughput KCNA pipeline, balancing isolation, latency, and dynamic scaling under bursty traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant token-bucket quotas and fair queuing
- Backpressure signaling (429s, retry-after) and quota persistence
- Telemetry-driven dynamic rebalancing and burst forgiveness
- Canary-based validation and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  tryConsume(n = 1) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

